  "$comment": "Deterministic, hand-curated recommendations for the lab builder wizard. Nothing here is scored by a model, so every pre-selected topic can show the exact reason it was chosen. `levels` lists the 1st-party topics that make up a lab at each level (the new depth that level adds; prerequisites are added automatically, so a level 200 lab still includes the level 100 foundations it depends on). `verticals` and `departments` add 1st-party topics that matter to that industry or team; they are recommended only at the chosen level, and every one stays selectable at its level. 3rd-party SaaS/ERP/CRM/EHR connector topics (`thirdPartyConnector: true` in features.json) are never listed in `levels` or `topics` so custom labs default strictly to 1st-party Microsoft connectors; optional `optionalThirdParty` on a vertical or department notes relevant 3rd-party connectors as unchecked options in Step 6 without selecting or recommending them by default. Features that do not apply to the chosen products (or, for Copilot Studio, the chosen harness) are ignored, so one list serves every product combination and every harness. Every id must exist in the catalog (validateConcepts enforces this).",
